  composite tailIncomplete and the instant path refuses to copy it.
  THE RAW CHANNELS ARE FIXED TOO (P0-tail-raw), and their fix is the OPPOSITE of the composite's.
  The composite could stop painting; a raw channel's source is a live device, and ending its TRACK
  makes Chrome stop the recorder itself and discard the backlog (measured: 622 ms still missing). So
  the source is STARVED — 1 fps, same frame size — and then drained: 1344 ms missing → 7-216 ms at
  4K, 7-27 ms at 1080p, twice each. `npm run oracle:load` now runs both phases. The stop path also
  grew deadlines everywhere, including the composite's own stop: a take whose recorders are all deaf
  to stop() now comes back in 5.6 s with every channel on disk, where it used to hang forever.
  Audio stops at the press rather than after the drain — with it stopping late, one take measured
  mic 11947 ms against a screen channel of 10059 ms.
