- PERVASIVE AUDIO NOISE root-caused + fixed (2026-07-16): render mix bus summed all audio channels at UNITY (no headroom) — mic+system-audio sum clipped softLimitSample on 34% of samples (measured). Removing the composite export shortcut had moved ALL exports onto this unstaged sum. Fix: 1/N per-channel headroom (single source unchanged/unity; multi-source guaranteed no clip, −6dB, recover via later 2-pass normalize). Proven at mix site: 16586→0 limiter hits. Single-source fidelity unregressed (THD −68dB).
- STUCK "waiting for mic" — hit AGAIN 2026-08-23 (PO: unresponsive, mic indicator still lit after
  refresh), fixed and PO-VERIFIED ("record seems to be okay"). The 2026-07-24 fix bounded each arming
  STEP; what hung was the JOINS between them (`await src.settled`, `await Promise.all(armPromises)`),
  which had no deadline — so the arming label, which only updates when a step STARTS, sat on
  "Waiting for microphone…" wherever the hang actually was. Four fixes, all additive: budgets on both
  joins (take starts with whatever is ready); a deadline on every durable-worker round trip (a worker
  that never answered hung arm(), which opens a write stream per channel); createCaptureSession takes
  an AbortSignal and the record button becomes CANCEL while arming (it used to be disabled — that is
  what "unresponsive" meant); and a pagehide guard that stops tracks, because nothing released devices
  when the page went away. Measured: cancel returns in 416 ms, pre-aborted in 1 ms, a normal take arms
  in 228 ms with zero live tracks after stop. Regression cover: `npm run exp -- armcancel`.
  WHICH step originally wedged is still unknown — the label could not say. The failure MODE is gone,
  not the specific wedge; if it recurs the arming timeline + budget warnings will name it.
