  canvas.captureStream 30fps, <video>→drawImage ~56/s, MediaRecorder ~110KB/s all UNAFFECTED by hidden — the composite
  pipeline does not freeze, so a frozen file means the SOURCE stopped. Also measured: a tab under capture never goes
  hidden (Chrome force-renders it), and a static surface still yields ~1 keep-alive frame/s — so "no frame for 3s" = dead,
  not idle. Ship: src/core/capture/sourceLiveness.ts (pure, unit-tested) sampled from the composite's worklet tick →
  channel-stalled/channel-resumed events + sticky red capture banner (a toast is unseen — the user is in another tab) +
  Recording.stalled; composite marked UNUSABLE (kept running so it keeps watching; cancelled at stop) so an unedited
  export renders from the raw channels instead of copying still frames. Same treatment when a video track ENDS mid-take —
  previously readyState stayed 2, the composite repainted the last frame forever and instant export copied it (real bug).
